---
name: x-bookmark-digest-files
description: >-
  Use when x-bookmark-digest needs fill-page.py, page-template.tsx or
  sample-digest.json and they are not beside its SKILL.md (e.g. an imported
  bot): holds those helper files to write out.
---
Purpose: ships the helper files for `x-bookmark-digest` (fill-page.py, page-template.tsx, sample-digest.json) so an imported bot can recreate them byte-for-byte.
Version: x-bookmark-digest-files v1 (2026-10-23), matches x-bookmark-digest section 5.
## Setup (only if the helpers are not beside x-bookmark-digest/SKILL.md)

1. Pick a working folder: `bd-tools/` in your own store (e.g. `/cursor/stores/<your-store-id>/bd-tools/`) if you have one, else `/workspace/bd-tools/`. Run `mkdir -p <folder> && cd <folder>`.
2. Write the files. Pick one method:
   - **Method A, preferred if this skill's text is on disk** (e.g. `.../x-bookmark-digest-files/SKILL.md`). Run one python one-liner that cuts each file out between its `<!-- FILE: name -->` marker and its `<!-- END FILE -->` marker (the fence lines are dropped). The regex writes backticks as `\x60`, which keeps bash from treating them as command substitution:
     `python3 -c "import re,sys;t=open(sys.argv[1]).read();[open(n,'w').write(b if n!='sample-digest.json' else b[:-1]) for n,b in re.findall(r'<!-- FILE: (\S+) -->\n\x60{4}\w*\n(.*?)\x60{4}\n<!-- END FILE -->',t,re.S)]" /path/to/x-bookmark-digest-files/SKILL.md`
   - **Method B, primary for imported bots (skill not on disk).** For each file, run one Shell command with a quoted heredoc. Paste the fenced block content exactly, with nothing added, removed or re-indented:
     - `cat > fill-page.py <<'BDEOF'` + content + a line `BDEOF`
     - `cat > page-template.tsx <<'BDEOF'` + content + a line `BDEOF`
     - `python3 -c "import sys;sys.stdout.write(sys.stdin.read()[:-1])" > sample-digest.json <<'BDEOF'` + content + a line `BDEOF` (this file has no trailing newline, and the wrapper drops the one the heredoc adds)
     The quoted `'BDEOF'` stops all `$`, backtick and backslash expansion. No file contains `BDEOF`.
3. Verify: `sha256sum fill-page.py page-template.tsx sample-digest.json` must match the hashes below. Then run `chmod +x fill-page.py`.
4. Self-check: `python3 fill-page.py sample-digest.json > /tmp/t.tsx && echo OK` must print OK.
5. In x-bookmark-digest section 5, run every command from this folder, e.g. `python3 <folder>/fill-page.py ...`. fill-page.py finds page-template.tsx beside itself.

Expected sha256:
- `fill-page.py` 0377f682518800c67ff99da781c222b5b4acb3378b33db7f5a42b58c5e8eaf11
- `page-template.tsx` 64044cb86aa2905a201b31bd924f7c914198bfcbefe8b4583e723457b407249e
- `sample-digest.json` 0798f47004260ba6ba712b396999a39b57b7a909c5f3e197ea188bb11ca7215a

## Files

### fill-page.py
<!-- FILE: fill-page.py -->
````python
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Bookmark Digest page builder (C2 layout). Run from anywhere; reads page-template.tsx next to this file.

Modes
  fill-page.py digest.json                 Full fill (1-3 saves / fast preview): prints a complete Page.
  fill-page.py --skeleton N header.json    Prints a skeleton Page with slots /*E1*/ .. /*EN*/, one per line.
                                           header.json = {"title","subtitle","type","themesLine"} (entries ignored).
  fill-page.py --entry entry.json          Prints the exact one-line slot replacement: {...},
                                           Use it as EditCanvas new_string with old_string "/*En*/".
  fill-page.py --check-entry line.txt      Validates a hand-made slot line (exit 1 + reason if broken).
Options
  --rewrite-colours   Also rewrite "colour/colour" pairs (e.g. "orange/black" -> "orange and black").
                      Not needed for compiling (see SKILL.md); purely cosmetic.

Why escaping matters: an entry string that is not escaped (a raw " in the text) ends the JS string early, so
words after it become code. tsc then fails with TS1005 "',' expected" or TS2304/TS2552
"Cannot find name 'orange'" / "'black'". That is what looked like a "colour word" rejection. json.dumps
always escapes correctly, so never hand-type entry lines.
"""
import json, re, sys, pathlib

HERE = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
TPL = HERE / "page-template.tsx"
FIELDS = ["n", "title", "author", "postedDate", "url", "bucket", "tags", "type", "readMin", "summary",
          "keyPoints", "quote", "threadSteps", "media", "details", "whyItMatters", "nextStep", "sensitive", "flags"]
DEFAULTS = {"tags": [], "readMin": 1, "summary": [], "keyPoints": [], "quote": "", "threadSteps": [], "media": [],
            "details": [], "whyItMatters": "", "nextStep": "", "sensitive": False, "flags": []}
HEADER_KEYS = ["title", "subtitle", "type", "themesLine"]
COLOURS = ("black white grey gray red orange yellow green blue purple pink brown cyan magenta teal navy "
           "gold silver olive maroon lime violet indigo beige tan").split()
CPAIR = re.compile(r"\b(" + "|".join(COLOURS) + r")/(" + "|".join(COLOURS) + r")\b", re.I)


def die(msg):
    sys.stderr.write("fill-page.py: " + msg + "\n"); sys.exit(1)


def clean_text(s, rewrite):
    s = s.replace("\r\n", "\n").replace("\r", "\n")
    s = s.replace("\u2028", " ").replace("\u2029", " ")          # JS line separators break string literals
    s = re.sub(r"[\x00-\x08\x0b\x0c\x0e-\x1f]", "", s)            # control chars
    if rewrite:
        s = CPAIR.sub(lambda m: f"{m.group(1)} and {m.group(2)}", s)
    return s


def walk(v, rewrite):
    if isinstance(v, str): return clean_text(v, rewrite)
    if isinstance(v, list): return [walk(x, rewrite) for x in v]
    if isinstance(v, dict): return {k: walk(x, rewrite) for k, x in v.items()}
    return v


def dump(v):
    # ensure_ascii=False keeps — → · emoji literal; "</" escaped so nothing can close a tag early.
    return json.dumps(v, ensure_ascii=False).replace("</", "<\\/")


def norm_entry(e, rewrite, n=None):
    if not isinstance(e, dict): die("entry must be a JSON object")
    if n is not None: e = {**e, "n": n}
    missing = [k for k in ("n", "title", "author", "url") if k not in e]
    if missing: die(f"entry missing {missing}")
    if not isinstance(e["n"], int) or e["n"] < 1: die("n must be a positive integer")
    out = {k: e.get(k, DEFAULTS.get(k, "")) for k in FIELDS}
    extra = {k: v for k, v in e.items() if k not in FIELDS}
    out.update(extra)
    return walk(out, rewrite)


def entry_line(e, rewrite):
    line = dump(norm_entry(e, rewrite)) + ","
    check_line(line)
    return line


def check_line(line):
    s = line.strip()
    if "\n" in s: return "contains a newline"
    if not s.endswith(","): return "must end with a comma"
    try: obj = json.loads(s[:-1])
    except Exception as ex: return f"not valid JSON: {ex}"
    if not isinstance(obj, dict): return "not an object"
    miss = [k for k in FIELDS if k not in obj]
    if miss: return f"missing fields {miss}"
    if re.search(r"/\*E\d+\*/", s): return "contains a slot marker like /*E3*/ — rephrase"
    if "\u2028" in s or "\u2029" in s: return "contains U+2028/2029"
    return None


def header_obj(h, rewrite):
    for k in ("title",):
        if k not in h: die(f"header missing {k}")
    return walk({k: h.get(k, "") for k in HEADER_KEYS}, rewrite)


def render(header, slot_lines):
    tpl = TPL.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    hd = dump(header)[:-1]  # drop closing brace
    body = hd + ",\n \"entries\": [\n" + "".join("  " + l + "\n" for l in slot_lines) + " ]}"
    out, k = re.subn(r"/\*DIGEST_START\*/.*?/\*DIGEST_END\*/",
                     lambda m: "/*DIGEST_START*/" + body + "/*DIGEST_END*/", tpl, flags=re.S)
    if k != 1: die("DIGEST markers not found in page-template.tsx")
    return out


def load(p):
    try: return json.load(open(p, encoding="utf-8"))
    except Exception as ex: die(f"cannot read {p}: {ex}")


def main(argv):
    rewrite = "--rewrite-colours" in argv
    a = [x for x in argv if x != "--rewrite-colours"]
    if not a: die(__doc__)
    if a[0] == "--skeleton":
        if len(a) != 3: die("usage: --skeleton N header.json")
        n = int(a[1]); h = header_obj(load(a[2]), rewrite)
        if not 1 <= n <= 100: die("N must be 1..100")
        sys.stdout.write(render(h, [f"/*E{i}*/" for i in range(1, n + 1)]))
    elif a[0] == "--entry":
        if len(a) != 2: die("usage: --entry entry.json")
        sys.stdout.write(entry_line(load(a[1]), rewrite) + "\n")
    elif a[0] == "--check-entry":
        line = open(a[1], encoding="utf-8").read().rstrip("\n")
        err = check_line(line)
        if err: die("bad slot line: " + err)
        print("ok")
    else:
        d = load(a[0])
        if "title" not in d or "entries" not in d: die("digest needs title and entries")
        lines = [entry_line(e, rewrite) for e in d["entries"]]
        ns = [json.loads(l[:-1])["n"] for l in lines]
        if len(set(ns)) != len(ns): die("duplicate n values")
        sys.stdout.write(render(header_obj(d, rewrite), lines))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main(sys.argv[1:])
````
<!-- END FILE -->

### page-template.tsx
<!-- FILE: page-template.tsx -->
````tsx
import { useState, Page as GPage } from "grok/canvas";
// ==== DATA: generated by fill-page.py; never hand-edit the render code below ====
const DIGEST: any = /*DIGEST_START*/{"title": "Bookmark Digest", "subtitle": "0 saves", "type": "posts", "themesLine": "",
 "entries": [
  /*ENTRIES*/
 ]}/*DIGEST_END*/;
// ==== RENDER: never edit below ====
const arr=(x:any)=>Array.isArray(x)?x:(x?[x]:[]);
const mix=(p:number)=>`color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ${p}%, transparent)`;
function inl(s:string,k:string){const out:any[]=[];const re=/(\*\*[^*]+\*\*|\*[^*]+\*|`[^`]+`|\[[^\]]+\]\([^)]+\))/g;let last=0,i=0;let m:RegExpExecArray|null;
 while((m=re.exec(s||""))){if(m.index>last)out.push(s.slice(last,m.index));const t=m[0];
  if(t.startsWith("**"))out.push(<b key={k+i++}>{t.slice(2,-2)}</b>);else if(t.startsWith("`"))out.push(<code key={k+i++} style={{fontSize:"0.9em",padding:"1px 5px",borderRadius:4,background:mix(12)}}>{t.slice(1,-1)}</code>);
  else if(t.startsWith("[")){const mm=/\[([^\]]+)\]\(([^)]+)\)/.exec(t)!;out.push(<a key={k+i++} href={mm[2]} target="_blank" style={{color:"inherit",textDecorationColor:mix(55),textUnderlineOffset:3}}>{mm[1]}</a>);}else out.push(<i key={k+i++}>{t.slice(1,-1)}</i>);
  last=m.index+t.length;}
 if(last<(s||"").length)out.push(s.slice(last));return out;}
function List({items,k,mark}:{items:any[];k:string;mark?:string}){return <div style={{margin:"4px 0"}}>{items.map((t,i)=><div key={k+i} style={{display:"flex",gap:10,margin:"6px 0",lineHeight:1.6}}><span style={{opacity:0.6,flexShrink:0}}>{mark||"–"}</span><span>{inl(String(t),k+i)}</span></div>)}</div>;}
function Steps({steps,k,c}:{steps:any[];k:string;c:any}){return <div style={{margin:"8px 0"}}>{steps.map((t,i)=>
 <div key={k+i} style={{display:"flex",gap:14}}>
  <div style={{display:"flex",flexDirection:"column",alignItems:"center"}}>
   <div style={{width:c.size,height:c.size,borderRadius:c.radius??"50%",background:c.bg,color:c.fg,display:"flex",alignItems:"center",justifyContent:"center",fontSize:c.fs||12,fontWeight:700,flexShrink:0,fontFamily:c.font}}>{c.label?c.label(i):i+1}</div>
   {i<steps.length-1&&<div style={{width:c.lw||2,flex:1,minHeight:12,background:mix(c.lo||18),...(c.dash?{background:"none",borderLeft:`2px dashed ${mix(30)}`,width:0}:{})}}/>}
  </div>
  <div style={{paddingBottom:16,paddingTop:Math.max(0,(c.size-24)/2),lineHeight:1.6}}>{inl(String(t),k+i)}</div>
 </div>)}</div>;}
function Body({e,H,c,q,mark}:{e:any;H:(t:string)=>any;c:any;q:any;mark?:string}){const k="e"+e.n;return <div>
 {arr(e.summary).map((p:string,i:number)=><p key={i} style={{margin:"0 0 12px",lineHeight:1.7}}>{inl(p,k+"s"+i)}</p>)}
 {e.quote&&<blockquote style={{margin:"16px 0",...q}}>“{e.quote}”</blockquote>}
 {arr(e.keyPoints).length>0&&<>{H("Key points")}<List items={arr(e.keyPoints)} k={k+"k"} mark={mark}/></>}
 {arr(e.threadSteps).length>0&&<>{H("Thread, step by step")}<Steps steps={arr(e.threadSteps)} k={k+"t"} c={c}/></>}
 {arr(e.media).length>0&&<>{H(DIGEST.type==="videos"?"What the video shows":"What the media shows")}<List items={arr(e.media)} k={k+"m"} mark={mark}/></>}
 {arr(e.details).length>0&&<>{H("Details")}<List items={arr(e.details)} k={k+"d"} mark={mark}/></>}
 {e.whyItMatters&&<>{H("Why it matters")}<p style={{margin:"4px 0",lineHeight:1.65}}>{inl(e.whyItMatters,k+"w")}</p></>}
 {e.nextStep&&<>{H("Next step")}<p style={{margin:"4px 0",lineHeight:1.65}}>{inl(e.nextStep,k+"n")}</p></>}
</div>;}
function Fold({e,children,st}:{e:any;children:any;st?:any}){return e.sensitive?<details style={{margin:"8px 0"}}><summary style={{cursor:"pointer",opacity:0.8,...st}}>Sensitive content — click to show (text only)</summary>{children}</details>:children;}
function useF(){const [bk,setBk]=useState("All");const [tg,setTg]=useState("All");const E:any[]=arr(DIGEST.entries);
 const buckets=["All",...Array.from(new Set(E.map(d=>d.bucket)))] as string[];const tags=["All",...Array.from(new Set(E.flatMap(d=>arr(d.tags))))] as string[];
 const shown=E.filter(d=>(bk==="All"||d.bucket===bk)&&(tg==="All"||arr(d.tags).includes(tg)));return {bk,setBk,tg,setTg,buckets,tags,shown,E};}
const btn:any={border:"none",background:"transparent",color:"inherit",cursor:"pointer",font:"inherit"};
const T:any={kicker:"Your saves",head:"Bookmark Digest",font:"'D-DIN', 'Helvetica Neue', Inter, 'Segoe UI', system-ui, Arial, sans-serif",num:"'D-DIN', 'Helvetica Neue', Inter, 'Segoe UI', system-ui, Arial, sans-serif",track:"0.14em",lw:400,vw:400,bw:400,ns:56,nw:0,ts:22,tw:400,tt:"-0.005em",tc:"none",hs:44,hw:300,ht:"-0.01em",rule:14,rp:48,br:4,center:true,mark:"·",
 q:{textAlign:"center",fontSize:22,fontWeight:380,lineHeight:1.45,padding:"8px 0"},c:{size:28,bg:mix(11),fs:12,lo:18,lw:1}};
const SP=[0,4,8,12,16,24,32,48,64,96];
const L=(o?:any)=>({fontSize:10.5,letterSpacing:T.track,textTransform:"uppercase",opacity:0.68,fontWeight:T.lw,...o});
const HR=(t:string)=><div style={{...L(),margin:`${SP[7]}px 0 ${SP[3]}px`,paddingTop:SP[4],borderTop:`1px solid ${mix(T.rule)}`,textAlign:T.center?"center":"left"}}>{t}</div>;
function Spec({e}:{e:any}){const s=[["Author",e.author],["Posted",e.postedDate],["Format",e.type],["Read",`${e.readMin} min`],["Bucket",e.bucket],["Tags",arr(e.tags).join(" · ")||"—"]];
 return <div style={{display:"grid",gridTemplateColumns:"repeat(auto-fit,minmax(130px,1fr))",gap:`${SP[5]}px ${SP[6]}px`,padding:`${SP[5]}px 0`,borderTop:`1px solid ${mix(T.rule)}`,borderBottom:`1px solid ${mix(T.rule)}`,textAlign:T.center?"center":"left"}}>
  {s.map(([k,v])=><div key={k}><div style={L({marginBottom:SP[2]})}>{k}</div><div style={{fontSize:14,fontWeight:T.vw,fontFamily:k==="Posted"||k==="Read"?T.num:T.font}}>{v}</div></div>)}</div>;}
function Row({e,open,tog}:{e:any;open:boolean;tog:()=>void}){return <div id={"s"+e.n} style={{borderBottom:`1px solid ${mix(T.rule)}`}}>
 <button onClick={tog} style={{...btn,display:"grid",gridTemplateColumns:T.center?"1fr":`${T.nw}px 1fr auto`,gap:SP[6],width:"100%",textAlign:T.center?"center":"left",padding:`${T.rp}px ${SP[2]}px`,alignItems:"center"}}>
  <span style={{fontFamily:T.num,fontSize:T.ns,fontWeight:200,lineHeight:1,opacity:open?0.95:0.55,letterSpacing:"-0.02em",fontVariantNumeric:"tabular-nums"}}>{String(e.n).padStart(2,"0")}</span>
  <span><span style={L({display:"block",marginBottom:SP[3]})}>{e.bucket} <span style={{opacity:0.7}}>/</span> {e.postedDate} <span style={{opacity:0.7}}>/</span> {e.readMin} min</span>
   <span style={{display:"block",fontSize:T.ts,fontWeight:T.tw,lineHeight:1.3,letterSpacing:T.tt,textTransform:T.tc}}>{e.title}</span>
   <span style={{display:"block",fontSize:13,opacity:0.72,marginTop:SP[3],fontWeight:T.vw}}>{e.author}{arr(e.tags).length?"   ·   "+arr(e.tags).map((t:string)=>"#"+t).join("  "):""}{arr(e.flags).length?`   ·   ⚑ ${arr(e.flags).length}`:""}</span></span>
  {!T.center&&<span style={L({opacity:0.75,whiteSpace:"nowrap"})}>{open?"Close —":"Open +"}</span>}
 </button>
 {open&&<div style={{padding:`0 ${SP[2]}px ${SP[8]}px`,paddingLeft:T.center?SP[2]:T.nw+SP[6]+SP[2],fontSize:15,fontWeight:T.bw,maxWidth:T.center?620:"none",margin:T.center?"0 auto":0}}>
  <Spec e={e}/>
  {arr(e.flags).length>0&&<div style={{...L({opacity:0.85}),margin:`${SP[5]}px 0 0`,textAlign:T.center?"center":"left"}}>⚑ {arr(e.flags).join("   ·   ")}</div>}
  <div style={{marginTop:SP[6]}}><Fold e={e} st={L()}><Body e={e} H={HR} mark={T.mark} q={T.q} c={T.c}/></Fold></div>
  <div style={{marginTop:SP[7],textAlign:T.center?"center":"left"}}><a href={e.url} target="_blank" style={{...L({opacity:0.9,fontWeight:600}),color:"inherit",textDecoration:"none",display:"inline-block",padding:`${SP[3]}px ${SP[5]}px`,borderRadius:T.br,background:mix(12)}}>Open post on X  →</a></div></div>}
</div>;}
export default function Page(){const f=useF();const [op,setOp]=useState<number[]>([]);
 const tog=(n:number)=>setOp(op.includes(n)?op.filter(x=>x!==n):[...op,n]);
 const seg=(v:string,cur:string,set:any)=><button key={v} onClick={()=>set(v)} style={{...btn,...L({opacity:v===cur?1:0.62,fontWeight:v===cur?600:T.lw}),padding:`${SP[2]}px ${SP[3]}px`,margin:`0 ${SP[1]}px ${SP[2]}px 0`,borderRadius:T.br,background:v===cur?mix(15):"transparent"}}>{v}</button>;
 return <GPage title={DIGEST.title}><div style={{maxWidth:860,margin:"0 auto",fontFamily:T.font,padding:`${SP[5]}px 0 ${SP[9]}px`}}>
  <div style={{textAlign:T.center?"center":"left",padding:`${SP[6]}px 0 ${SP[7]}px`}}>
   <div style={L({marginBottom:SP[4]})}>{T.kicker} · {DIGEST.subtitle}</div>
   <div style={{fontSize:T.hs,fontWeight:T.hw,letterSpacing:T.ht,textTransform:T.tc,lineHeight:1.1}}>{T.head}</div>
   {DIGEST.themesLine&&<div style={{marginTop:SP[4],fontSize:15,opacity:0.8,fontWeight:T.vw}}>{inl(DIGEST.themesLine,"th")}</div>}</div>
  <div style={{display:"grid",gridTemplateColumns:"72px 1fr",gap:`${SP[3]}px ${SP[4]}px`,alignItems:"baseline",padding:`${SP[5]}px 0`,borderTop:`1px solid ${mix(T.rule)}`}}>
   <span style={L()}>Bucket</span><div>{f.buckets.map(b=>seg(b,f.bk,f.setBk))}</div>
   <span style={L()}>Tag</span><div>{f.tags.map(t=>seg(t,f.tg,f.setTg))}</div></div>
  <div style={{display:"flex",justifyContent:"space-between",padding:`${SP[4]}px ${SP[2]}px`,borderTop:`1px solid ${mix(T.rule)}`,borderBottom:`1px solid ${mix(T.rule)}`}}>
   <span style={L()}><span style={{fontFamily:T.num}}>{String(f.shown.length).padStart(2,"0")} / {String(f.E.length).padStart(2,"0")}</span>  saves</span>
   <span><button style={{...btn,...L({opacity:0.82})}} onClick={()=>setOp(f.shown.map(d=>d.n))}>Expand all</button><span style={{margin:`0 ${SP[3]}px`,opacity:0.45}}>|</span><button style={{...btn,...L({opacity:0.82})}} onClick={()=>setOp([])}>Collapse all</button></span></div>
  {f.shown.length===0&&<p style={{...L(),padding:SP[7],textAlign:"center"}}>No entries match these filters</p>}
  {f.shown.map(d=><Row key={d.n} e={d} open={op.includes(d.n)} tog={()=>tog(d.n)}/>)}
 </div></GPage>;}
````
